module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Thickenings.LiftDifferenceSquareZeroValues

/-!
# The difference of two morphisms agreeing on a first order thickening

Let `Z ⊂ X` be a first order thickening of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S`, with inclusion
`i : Z ⟶ X`, let `W₀ ⊆ W` be a closed subspace of a second algebraic space, with inclusion
`j : W₀ ⟶ W`, let `e₀ : Z ⟶ W₀` be a morphism and let `c, c' : X ⟶ W` be two morphisms whose
restrictions to the thickening are both `e₀ ≫ j`.

`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/Thickenings/LiftDifferenceRestrictedTarget.lean` reads the
two comorphisms as morphisms of sheaves of rings

`j^{-1}𝒪_W ⟶ (e₀)_*(i^{-1}𝒪_X)`

on the small étale site of `W₀`, and
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/Thickenings/LiftDifferenceSquareZeroValues.lean` assembles
the ideal of values `(e₀)_*𝒞_{Z/X}` they differ in.  This file puts the two together into a
`Stacks.Sites.LiftDifferenceData` for the quotient map `j^♯ : j^{-1}𝒪_W ⟶ 𝒪_{W₀}`.

Four of the five fields are discharged here.  The fifth — that the two comorphisms agree on the
sections killed by `j^♯`, hypothesis (2) of [Stacks Project, Tag 0618] — is *not* a consequence
of the data assembled so far: it says that the two morphisms agree to first order along the
ideal of `W₀` in `W`, which in the situation of [Stacks Project, Tag 0CKE] holds because both
`c` and `c'` are sections of one and the same morphism `W ⟶ X` and the ideal of `W₀` is
generated by the functions pulled back along it.  It is therefore a hypothesis of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedLiftDifferenceData`; it is enough to check it on a
*generating family*, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSharpThroughThickening_app_eq_of_mem_span`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSharpDiff`: the sectionwise difference of the two
  transported comorphisms, read in the ideal of values.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedLiftDifferenceData`: **the difference of the two
  transported comorphisms**, as a `Stacks.Sites.LiftDifferenceData` for `j^♯` with the ideal of
  values of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSquareZeroValues`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSharpThroughThickening_comp_reduction_structureSharp`: the
  transported comorphism of `c`, followed by the direct image of the reduction
  `i^{-1}𝒪_X ⟶ 𝒪_Z`, is `j^♯` followed by the comorphism of `e₀`.  This is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSharpThroughThickening_comp_reduction` read through
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedStructureSharpReduction_eq`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_restrictedSquareZeroValues_ι_eq`: **the sectionwise difference
  of the two transported comorphisms is a section of the ideal of values.**  Their difference is
  killed by the reduction, by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSharpThroughThickening_comp_reduction_eq`, and the image of
  the ideal of values is exactly what the reduction kills, by
  `Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPullback.exists_app_pullbackModuleMap_eq` at
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.conormalInverseImageι`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSquareZeroValues_ι_smul`: the `𝒪_{W₀}`-action on the ideal
  of values is the multiplication by the transported comorphism of `c`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSquareZeroValues_ι_restrictedSharpDiff`: the defining
  equation of the difference.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSharpThroughThickening_app_eq_of_mem_span`: **hypothesis
  (2) of [Stacks Project, Tag 0618] from a generating family of the kernel of `j^♯`**, which is
  `Stacks.Sites.app_eq_of_app_eq_zero_of_mem_span` at the data assembled here.

## Implementation notes

**The difference is defined by choice.**  The field `diff` of
`Stacks.Sites.LiftDifferenceData` is a function into the module of values, and what the
exactness of the ideal sequence supplies is an existence statement; so `diff` is the chosen
preimage, pinned by the field `ι_diff`.  The choice is unique, the inclusion being injective on
sections.

**The left exactness of the direct image is introduced by name**, as in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/Thickenings/LiftDifferenceSquareZeroValues.lean`:
instance search does not find it for the direct image of a morphism of topoi on its own.

**The `𝒪_{W₀}`-action on the sections of the ideal of values is seated by a `letI` naming the
canonical module structure `CategoryTheory.ModuleCat.isModule`**, rather than left to instance
search, in the statement of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSquareZeroValues_ι_smul`.  The sheaf of rings indexing the
module is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf`, a plain `def`, so the `Semiring` and
`AddCommMonoid` arguments that search assembles for the goal at this spelling agree with the
ones the section module's own structure carries only after that `def` is unfolded, which
instance search — working at `instances` transparency — will not do, and the canonical candidate
is rejected during unification.  The bound value is term-identical to the canonical instance, so
no second module structure exists, and `letI` zeta-reduces, so the statement is the same one.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0618](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0618), the difference of two
  lifts.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04CN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04CN), the conormal module.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CKE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CKE)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPullback Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPushforward

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
  {X W : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1)
  (W₀ : ClosedSubspaces B S hS W.1)
  (e₀ : (⟨Z.1.toFunctor, Z.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) ⟶
      (⟨W₀.1.toFunctor, W₀.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS))

/-- **The reduction of the transported comorphism of `c` is `j^♯` followed by the comorphism of
`e₀`.**  Both sides are morphisms `j^{-1}𝒪_W ⟶ (e₀)_*𝒪_Z`:
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSharpThroughThickening_comp_reduction` computes the left hand
side as `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedStructureSharpReduction`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedStructureSharpReduction_eq` factors that through `j^♯`. -/
theorem restrictedSharpThroughThickening_comp_reduction_structureSharp (c : X ⟶ W)
    (h : subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z ≫ c = e₀ ≫ subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀) :
    restrictedSharpThroughThickening B S hS Z W₀ c e₀ h ≫
        pullbackRingSheafMap
          (SmallEtale.topology B S hS
            (⟨W₀.1.toFunctor, W₀.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS).1)
          (smallToposMorphismTypeU B S hS e₀).pushforward
          (structureSharpRingInverseImage B S hS (subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z)) =
      structureSharpRingInverseImage B S hS (subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀) ≫
        structureSharp B S hS e₀ :=
  (restrictedSharpThroughThickening_comp_reduction B S hS Z W₀ c e₀ h).trans
    (restrictedStructureSharpReduction_eq B S hS Z W₀ e₀)

variable (hZ : IsFirstOrderThickening B S hS X Z.1)

/-- **The sectionwise difference of the two transported comorphisms is a section of the ideal of
values.**  The difference is killed by the direct image of the reduction
`i^{-1}𝒪_X ⟶ 𝒪_Z`, because both transported comorphisms become the transported comorphism of
`e₀ ≫ j` after it; and a section of `(e₀)_*(i^{-1}𝒪_X)` killed by that reduction is in the image
of `(e₀)_*𝒞_{Z/X}`, the conormal module being exactly the kernel of the reduction. -/
theorem exists_restrictedSquareZeroValues_ι_eq (c c' : X ⟶ W)
    (h : subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z ≫ c = e₀ ≫ subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)
    (h' : subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z ≫ c' = e₀ ≫ subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)
    (V : (SmallEtale B S hS (⟨W₀.1.toFunctor, W₀.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS).1)ᵒᵖ)
    (x : (structureRingSheafInverseImage B S hS
      (subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)).obj.obj V) :
    ∃ m : ((modulePushforward B S hS e₀).obj (conormalModule B S hS X Z)).val.obj V,
      (restrictedSquareZeroValues B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ).ι m =
        (restrictedSharpThroughThickening B S hS Z W₀ c e₀ h).hom.app V x -
          (restrictedSharpThroughThickening B S hS Z W₀ c' e₀ h').hom.app V x :=
  haveI := preservesFiniteLimits_smallToposMorphismTypeU_pushforward B S hS e₀
  exists_app_pullbackModuleMap_eq
    (SmallEtale.topology B S hS (⟨W₀.1.toFunctor, W₀.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS).1)
    (smallToposMorphismTypeU B S hS e₀).pushforward
    (conormalInverseImageι B S hS Z hZ)
    (structureSharpRingInverseImage B S hS (subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z)) V
    (app_conormalInverseImageι_eq_zero B S hS Z hZ)
    (conormalInverseImageι_injective B S hS Z hZ)
    (exists_conormalInverseImageι_eq B S hS Z hZ) _
    (Stacks.Sites.sub_mem_ker_of_comp_eq _ _ _
      (restrictedSharpThroughThickening_comp_reduction_eq B S hS Z W₀ c c' e₀ h h') V x)

/-- **The `𝒪_{W₀}`-action on the ideal of values is the multiplication by the transported
comorphism of `c`.**  The scalar `j^♯(x)` acts on `(e₀)_*𝒞_{Z/X}` through the comorphism of
`e₀`, and the transported comorphism of `c` has that same image under the reduction, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSharpThroughThickening_comp_reduction_structureSharp`; so
the two actions agree, and the inclusion of the ideal of values is linear for the
multiplication of the ambient sheaf of rings. -/
theorem restrictedSquareZeroValues_ι_smul (c : X ⟶ W)
    (h : subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z ≫ c = e₀ ≫ subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)
    {V : (SmallEtale B S hS (⟨W₀.1.toFunctor, W₀.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS).1)ᵒᵖ}
    (x : (structureRingSheafInverseImage B S hS
      (subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)).obj.obj V)
    (m : ((modulePushforward B S hS e₀).obj (conormalModule B S hS X Z)).val.obj V) :
    letI : Module ((structureRingSheaf B S hS
          (⟨W₀.1.toFunctor, W₀.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)).obj.obj V)
        (((modulePushforward B S hS e₀).obj (conormalModule B S hS X Z)).val.obj V) :=
      (((modulePushforward B S hS e₀).obj (conormalModule B S hS X Z)).val.obj V).isModule
    (restrictedSquareZeroValues B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ).ι
        ((structureSharpRingInverseImage B S hS
          (subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)).hom.app V x • m) =
      (show ToType ((restrictedSquareZeroValues B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ).ambient.obj.obj V) from
          (restrictedSharpThroughThickening B S hS Z W₀ c e₀ h).hom.app V x) *
        (restrictedSquareZeroValues B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ).ι m :=
  (congrArg (restrictedSquareZeroValues B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ).ι
      (smul_restrictScalars_pullbackModuleObj
        (SmallEtale.topology B S hS
          (⟨W₀.1.toFunctor, W₀.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS).1)
        (smallToposMorphismTypeU B S hS e₀).pushforward
        (structureSharpRingInverseImage B S hS (subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z))
        (conormalModule B S hS X Z) (structureSharp B S hS e₀) V _ _
        (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (congrArg (fun n => n.hom.app V)
          (restrictedSharpThroughThickening_comp_reduction_structureSharp
            B S hS Z W₀ e₀ c h)) x) m)).trans
    (mul_app_pullbackModuleMap
      (SmallEtale.topology B S hS
        (⟨W₀.1.toFunctor, W₀.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS).1)
      (smallToposMorphismTypeU B S hS e₀).pushforward
      (conormalInverseImageι B S hS Z hZ) V _ m)

/-- **The difference of the two transported comorphisms, as a section of the ideal of
values**: the preimage supplied by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_restrictedSquareZeroValues_ι_eq`, which
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSquareZeroValues_ι_restrictedSharpDiff` pins.  The choice is
unique, the inclusion of the ideal of values being injective on sections. -/
def restrictedSharpDiff (c c' : X ⟶ W)
    (h : subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z ≫ c = e₀ ≫ subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)
    (h' : subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z ≫ c' = e₀ ≫ subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)
    {V : (SmallEtale B S hS (⟨W₀.1.toFunctor, W₀.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS).1)ᵒᵖ}
    (x : (structureRingSheafInverseImage B S hS
      (subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)).obj.obj V) :
    ((modulePushforward B S hS e₀).obj (conormalModule B S hS X Z)).val.obj V :=
  (exists_restrictedSquareZeroValues_ι_eq B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ c c' h h' V x).choose

/-- The defining equation of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSharpDiff`. -/
theorem restrictedSquareZeroValues_ι_restrictedSharpDiff (c c' : X ⟶ W)
    (h : subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z ≫ c = e₀ ≫ subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)
    (h' : subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z ≫ c' = e₀ ≫ subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)
    {V : (SmallEtale B S hS (⟨W₀.1.toFunctor, W₀.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS).1)ᵒᵖ}
    (x : (structureRingSheafInverseImage B S hS
      (subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)).obj.obj V) :
    (restrictedSquareZeroValues B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ).ι
        (restrictedSharpDiff B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ c c' h h' x) =
      (restrictedSharpThroughThickening B S hS Z W₀ c e₀ h).hom.app V x -
        (restrictedSharpThroughThickening B S hS Z W₀ c' e₀ h').hom.app V x :=
  (exists_restrictedSquareZeroValues_ι_eq B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ c c' h h' V x).choose_spec

include hZ in
/-- **The two transported comorphisms agree on the sections killed by `j^♯`, from a generating
family.**  This is
`Stacks.Sites.app_eq_of_app_eq_zero_of_mem_span` at the data assembled above: the kernel of
`j^♯` only has to be generated, over a covering sieve, by sections it kills on which the two
comorphisms agree. -/
theorem restrictedSharpThroughThickening_app_eq_of_mem_span (c c' : X ⟶ W)
    (h : subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z ≫ c = e₀ ≫ subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)
    (h' : subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z ≫ c' = e₀ ≫ subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)
    (hgen : ∀ {V : (SmallEtale B S hS
        (⟨W₀.1.toFunctor, W₀.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS).1)ᵒᵖ}
      (x : (structureRingSheafInverseImage B S hS
        (subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)).obj.obj V),
      (structureSharpRingInverseImage B S hS
          (subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)).hom.app V x = 0 →
      ∃ T : Sieve V.unop, T ∈ SmallEtale.topology B S hS
          (⟨W₀.1.toFunctor, W₀.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS).1 V.unop ∧
        ∀ ⦃Y : SmallEtale B S hS
            (⟨W₀.1.toFunctor, W₀.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS).1⦄ (p : Y ⟶ V.unop), T p →
          (structureRingSheafInverseImage B S hS
              (subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)).obj.map p.op x ∈
            Ideal.span {y : (structureRingSheafInverseImage B S hS
                (subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)).obj.obj (op Y) |
              (structureSharpRingInverseImage B S hS
                  (subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)).hom.app (op Y) y = 0 ∧
                (restrictedSharpThroughThickening B S hS Z W₀ c e₀ h).hom.app (op Y) y =
                  (restrictedSharpThroughThickening B S hS Z W₀ c' e₀ h').hom.app (op Y) y})
    {V : (SmallEtale B S hS (⟨W₀.1.toFunctor, W₀.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS).1)ᵒᵖ}
    (x : (structureRingSheafInverseImage B S hS
      (subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)).obj.obj V)
    (hx : (structureSharpRingInverseImage B S hS
      (subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)).hom.app V x = 0) :
    (restrictedSharpThroughThickening B S hS Z W₀ c e₀ h).hom.app V x =
      (restrictedSharpThroughThickening B S hS Z W₀ c' e₀ h').hom.app V x :=
  Stacks.Sites.app_eq_of_app_eq_zero_of_mem_span
    (restrictedSquareZeroValues B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ)
    (restrictedSharpThroughThickening B S hS Z W₀ c e₀ h)
    (restrictedSharpThroughThickening B S hS Z W₀ c' e₀ h')
    (fun y m => restrictedSquareZeroValues_ι_smul B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ c h y m)
    (fun y => restrictedSharpDiff B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ c c' h h' y)
    (fun y => restrictedSquareZeroValues_ι_restrictedSharpDiff B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ c c' h h' y)
    (fun y hy => hgen y hy) x hx

/-- **The difference of two morphisms agreeing on a first order thickening.**  For two morphisms
`c, c' : X ⟶ W` whose restrictions to `Z` are both `e₀ ≫ j`, their transported comorphisms
`j^{-1}𝒪_W ⟶ (e₀)_*(i^{-1}𝒪_X)` are a pair of lifts into the square-zero ideal `(e₀)_*𝒞_{Z/X}`
of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSquareZeroValues`, for the quotient map
`j^♯ : j^{-1}𝒪_W ⟶ 𝒪_{W₀}`.

The hypothesis `hker` is hypothesis (2) of [Stacks Project, Tag 0618], that the two comorphisms
agree on the sections killed by `j^♯`; by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSharpThroughThickening_app_eq_of_mem_span` it is enough to
check it on a generating family of the kernel of `j^♯`. -/
def restrictedLiftDifferenceData (c c' : X ⟶ W)
    (h : subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z ≫ c = e₀ ≫ subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)
    (h' : subspaceInclusion B S hS X Z ≫ c' = e₀ ≫ subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)
    (hker : ∀ (V : (SmallEtale B S hS
        (⟨W₀.1.toFunctor, W₀.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS).1)ᵒᵖ)
      (x : (structureRingSheafInverseImage B S hS
        (subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)).obj.obj V),
      (structureSharpRingInverseImage B S hS
          (subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀)).hom.app V x = 0 →
        (restrictedSharpThroughThickening B S hS Z W₀ c e₀ h).hom.app V x =
          (restrictedSharpThroughThickening B S hS Z W₀ c' e₀ h').hom.app V x) :
    Stacks.Sites.LiftDifferenceData
      (structureSharpRingInverseImage B S hS (subspaceInclusion B S hS W W₀))
      (restrictedSquareZeroValues B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ) where
  f := restrictedSharpThroughThickening B S hS Z W₀ c e₀ h
  g := restrictedSharpThroughThickening B S hS Z W₀ c' e₀ h'
  ι_smul x m := restrictedSquareZeroValues_ι_smul B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ c h x m
  diff x := restrictedSharpDiff B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ c c' h h' x
  ι_diff x :=
    restrictedSquareZeroValues_ι_restrictedSharpDiff B S hS Z W₀ e₀ hZ c c' h h' x
  app_eq_of_app_eq_zero {V} x hx := hker V x hx

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
